---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { papers } from '../config';

const record = [
  "Building Ktema Systems end to end: the storage engine, the execution layer, and the governance layer as one system, and the coordinate addressing and state fabric beneath them. Four technical preprints in seven months.",
  'Rebuilt the payment core of a mobile banking app at Commerzbank (19.8M installs, BaFin, GDPR, PSD2), inside a roughly €700M transformation.',
  'Founded and bootstrapped StellarStep, shipping camera products over four years: Elie and Live Focus were both featured by Apple, MemoCam shipped on-photo text interaction years before Live Text, and Delta controlled a camera by coordinate rather than by menu, the principle Ktema now runs on.',
  "Led Android, web, desktop, and cloud work at Kakao, serving 45M+ monthly users, and built Korea's largest street-view VR map.",
  'Korean citizenship and German permanent residence, which let the founder work in both Asia and Europe.',
];
---

<Section
  id="founder"
  label="Founder"
  title="Taeho Lee"
  lede="Founder and first engineer, and the architect of the record format and the engine."
>
  <ul class="points">
    {record.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <div class="stack">
    <h3>Published research</h3>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The layers the engine stands on are documented in the open, so anyone can check them and
        build against them. The commercial layer inherits what survives that.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="papers">
      {
        papers.map((paper) => (
          <li>
            <a href={paper.href}>{paper.title}</a>
            <span class="papers__when">{paper.when}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .stack > * + * {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .papers {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .papers li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .papers__when {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }
</style>
